# Commands run by the launchd job com.redwood.demo (see com.redwood.demo.plist).
# RC_JOBS=rc.jobs.net28, REST=1 (with WIFID=1), MORE_JOBS="com.apple.bluetoothd com.apple.BlueTool",
# NILINJECT=Preferences CIINJECT=Preferences, connsys_step=17, XNU_SECS=150,
# applog=1 applog_name=Preferences.
#
# Run 96 (logs/lancelot-connsys48.log): Settings opened, the nil dictionary was built without its
# iconImage pair, and half a second later MobileIcons' icon rendering took the program down in
# +[CIContext contextWithOptions:] -- CoreImage's OpenGL ES back end with no EAGLContext (docs/metal.md,
# section 7). libredwood-ci.dylib now answers that request with a context over our OpenGL ES, and
# libredwood-gl.dylib goes into the process with it (build.sh, CIINJECT).
#
# One tap, then time to render the whole root list, then the picture: if the icons are drawn, the list
# is there and the next run can tap the Wi-Fi row; if something else dies, the console tail has it.
/redwood/bin/net_test wait 22
/redwood/bin/net_test dhcp en0 waitaddr en0 10
/redwood/bin/net_test fbwait 60
/redwood/bin/net_test wait 16
/redwood/bin/rwtouch swipe 0.5 0.985 0.5 0.3 200
/redwood/bin/net_test wait 3
/redwood/bin/rwtouch tap 0.543 0.712
/redwood/bin/net_test wait 8
/redwood/bin/net_test procs Preferences
/redwood/bin/fbgrab -log settings 300 0.5
/redwood/bin/net_test end